# Project pages carry a {% comment %} authoring block that Jekyll strips before
# it reaches the browser. Prettier formats .html with its HTML parser, which knows
# nothing about Liquid: it reads that block's example markup as real tags and
# reflows the whole block into nonsense (measured with prettier 3.8.0 and
# @shopify/prettier-plugin-liquid 1.10.0 -- the plugin only claims .liquid files).
# Every page built on _layouts/project_page.liquid is authored this way, so ignore
# the whole collection and keep those files formatted by hand.
_projects/*.html
